## How Speed Insights Works

### Automatic Data Collection
The SpeedInsights component automatically:
1. Detects when running on Vercel
2. Collects Web Vitals metrics (LCP, FID, CLS, FCP, TTFB, INP)
3. Sends anonymous performance data to Vercel
4. Works in production without additional configuration

### Environment Detection
- **Local Development**: Component is present but doesn't collect data
- **Vercel Deployment**: Automatically activates and collects metrics
- **Other Hosting**: Component is inert (no data collection)

## Integration with Existing Analytics

The project already has **Vercel Analytics** (`@vercel/analytics`) integrated:
```typescript
import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next';
// ... in layout
{process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production' && <Analytics />}
```

Speed Insights works seamlessly alongside Analytics:
- **Analytics**: Tracks page views and custom events
- **Speed Insights**: Tracks performance metrics and Web Vitals

Both components are independent and can be used together without conflicts.

## Next Steps for Deployment

To see Speed Insights data in your Vercel dashboard:

1. **Deploy to Vercel**
   ```bash
   vercel deploy
   ```

2. **Enable Speed Insights** (if not already enabled)
   - Go to your project in the Vercel dashboard
   - Navigate to Settings → Speed Insights
   - Enable the feature (may be enabled by default)

3. **Generate Traffic**
   - Visit your deployed site
   - Navigate through different pages
   - Real user metrics will be collected automatically

4. **View Insights**
   - Go to your project dashboard on Vercel
   - Click the "Speed Insights" tab
   - View performance metrics, Web Vitals scores, and page-specific data

## Technical Notes

### Performance Impact
- **Minimal**: ~1KB gzipped JavaScript
- **Async Loading**: Doesn't block page rendering
- **No Configuration Required**: Works out of the box

### Privacy
- All data is anonymous
- No personally identifiable information is collected
- Complies with privacy regulations (GDPR, CCPA)

### Browser Support
- Modern browsers with Web Vitals API support
- Gracefully degrades in older browsers
- No errors in unsupported environments

